  "root_cause": "Leap debugedit 5.0 emits Unknown DWARF DW_FORM_0x25 for indexed string forms in Clang 21 compiler-rt objects. PDFium links these distribution runtime objects even when its own translation units use DWARF4. debugedit 5.1 supports these indexed forms. A volatile __floattidf function pointer forces the exact runtime object into the standalone control.",
  "packaging_changes": [
    "Retain the six verified distribution patches and /usr/lib/rpm helper layout.",
    "Run the 35 upstream tests.",
    "Enable PIE using normal RPM compiler/linker flags; both installed executables are DYN.",
    "Use a lint-clean package description."
  ],
  "distribution_hardlink_patch_root": "The linked list is created only for a second scanned path with the same inode. An executable with a hardlink outside the RPM build root has st_nlink > 1 but no entry, and potentially no linked file. The inherited patch handles this normal absence. Both paired in-root links and outside-only links were exercised with real debug extraction, GDB indexing and executable runs.",
